{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1170887-dominatrix-haunt","id":1170887,"title":"Dominatrix Haunt","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-27T02:43:32-08:00","id":1170887,"title":"Dominatrix Haunt","content":"I know there's a general topic on the forum regarding ideas for how the Nosferatu clan curse may manifest. But how about specifically for a character who was a dominatrix in life? I don't mean that pseudo-erotic soft core Christian Grey BS either, but someone that makes their living off hardcore masochists ie people that get off on being cut, burnt, &quot;needleplay&quot;, etc. She also was someone that had a lot of issues, and was a self-cutter herself for eight years straight. I've been rolling ideas around in my head, but curious to see what others come up with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23641-tacotuesday","name":"TacoTuesday","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T03:10:31-08:00","id":1170890,"title":"","content":"I've always seen a dominant/dominatrix as almost an exclusively Ventrue/Daeva thing, Ventrue because of the dominance aspect and Daeva because of the sexual aspect, I can't see why a haunt would be interested in these things but then again there's Robyn Sloane from New Wave Requiem, whose Clan Bane didn't really have anything to do with her job.<br /> <br /> You can make it something about the character's demeanor that puts people off, also a tendency to wear latex suits is enough to give most people the heebie jeebies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T03:55:39-08:00","id":1170895,"title":"","content":"It's not really a sexual thing for her. She does it for supplemental income (long story how she got into it). And she doesn't go around wearing latex and PVC in public. In fact, she keeps what she does unknown to those around her, save for the small handful of clients she has.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23641-tacotuesday","name":"TacoTuesday","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T04:09:06-08:00","id":1170898,"title":"","content":"Can I ask what you mean by how &quot;curse manifests?&quot; It sounds like we're talking about appearance type things? <br /> <br /> Also, side note - there was a Nosferatu dom type in Night Horrors Immortal Sinners, if you have access to that book, if you want to mine that for ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T04:27:58-08:00","id":1170902,"title":"","content":"Kind of. Either how the Nosferatu in question &quot;warps&quot; or the environment around her does. Trying to stay away from the Masquerade style super deformities.<br /> <br /> No, I do not own that book yet.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23641-tacotuesday","name":"TacoTuesday","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T09:12:00-08:00","id":1170970,"title":"","content":"In VtR 2e, the Nosferatu bane is about relating to humans, as well as some fluff about having something 'creepy' about them in either appearance or demeanor.<br /> <br /> Could be as simple as coming off as alien (not extra-terrestrial so much as sticking out like a Satanist at a Catholic Mass) or predatory (like vampires often do, but more extreme). Given it's a Bane, she can give those sensations off without actually having to wear fetish gear in public. Could be eerily pale, if you want something more physical while still working as a dominatrix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T10:06:03-08:00","id":1170977,"title":"","content":"Could always go Hellraiser / Pinhead and co.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T11:18:42-08:00","id":1171000,"title":"","content":"The big thing about the the Lonely Curse is that it <i>always </i>makes the vampire unsettling. Of course, some people are &quot;into&quot; unsettling, so I don't see anything wrong with a Nosferatu dominatrix. Vampires are still people; just because she was Embraced by a Haunt doesn't mean she stops being into whatever she was into before.<br /> <br /> How about this for a curse?<br /> <br /> &quot;She always seems injured, though you'd be hard pressed to point to anything specific. Faint scars seem to line her skin, though they never really are in the same place when you look a second time. She walks with a slight limp, first favoring one leg, then the other, and both legs seem just a little too thin and bend just a little too far in the wrong ways. She rubs her fingers absent-mindedly, as if they'd been broken and the joints still ache, though it never seems to interfere in her holding anything. There, at the edge of clothes...is that a burn just peaking out from beneath the fabric? You can't really tell, and when she lifts her arm it simply reveals pale, smooth skin. That noise she made, that little sigh; didn't it sound just a little too hoarse?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T16:04:20-08:00","id":1171082,"title":"","content":"Vampire requiem New Wave. The Nos stand in character is a Dominatrix. She is on the back cover<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://images-na.ssl-images-amazon.com/images/I/913ElXNqMfL.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://images-na.ssl-images-amazon.com/images/I/913ElXNqMfL.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://images-na.ssl-images-amazon.com/images/I/913ElXNqMfL.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> https://images-na.ssl-images-amazon.com/images/I/913ElXNqMfL.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T17:31:02-08:00","id":1171109,"title":"","content":"I do actually own New Wave Requiem, but have not cracked it open yet. Will definitely do so now.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the replies all, still basically brainstorming this, so any reply is something to consider.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23641-tacotuesday","name":"TacoTuesday","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T16:51:15-08:00","id":1171370,"title":"","content":"I like that idea I had so much, I want to take it further. Her curse isn't just that people get this irrational impression that she's injured; each person perceives her as being injured in a way that has personal significance (in a negative way, of course) to them. It's not conscious or strong enough that they'll call her on it, as if she was mocking them or something, but it's enough to bring up feelings and memories that people would probably rather keep buried. Examples:<br /> <br /> <b>Bob</b> is an accountant, though he really wanted to be a professional cyclist. He always dreamed of competing in the Tour de France, but a knee infection when he was in college dashed those hopes. He has no problem in everyday life, but his right leg is <i>just</i> weak enough that he can never compete at that level. Whenever Bob is around the vampire (they frequent the same bar), he just can't shake the feeling that she <i>also</i> has a problem with her knee. He won't ask her about it, but it sticks in his mind, and makes him think about all those doctor's visits and frustrating sessions at the gym, as he tried (and failed) to regain his old form. It's enough that he's stopped hanging out with his friends, whenever they go to that bar.<br /> <br /> <b>Florence</b> is a cashier at a 24-hour big box grocery store. She lost her mother to cancer a few years ago, and has finally started to put the grief behind her. Only...there's this woman, who only comes in at night. She never buys any food - just odds and ends. What Florence can't stand is the way she scratches her throat, as it it's always bothering her. It's far too similar to how her mother used to scratch once the cancer started to spread. And there's this little sounds she makes- halfway between a cough and a sigh, so faint you almost can't hear it. Florence used to have nightmares about that sound, the one her mother made as she wasted away in that hospital bed.<br /> <br /> The best thing about it is that it can easily apply to the other player characters, too. It's an opportunity to ask each player a quick question: What's the worst injury your character ever received? And you can use the answer both as RP fuel between the vampire dom and her coterie and to expand everyones' backstories more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T14:50:49-08:00","id":1171633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1170887-dominatrix-haunt?p=1171000#post1171000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;She always seems injured, though you'd be hard pressed to point to anything specific. Faint scars seem to line her skin, though they never really are in the same place when you look a second time. She walks with a slight limp, first favoring one leg, then the other, and both legs seem just a little too thin and bend just a little too far in the wrong ways. She rubs her fingers absent-mindedly, as if they'd been broken and the joints still ache, though it never seems to interfere in her holding anything. There, at the edge of clothes...is that a burn just peaking out from beneath the fabric? You can't really tell, and when she lifts her arm it simply reveals pale, smooth skin. That noise she made, that little sigh; didn't it sound just a little too hoarse?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>like</i> that one.<br /> <br /> <br /> More generally, I think a Nosferatu dom might have a tendency to seem red-flaggy - like they always give off an air that they're not going to keep to their clients' limits or respect safewords. But it seems likely to me that such an air would seem like a plus to a client who knows it's an illusion - so they might have trouble attracting new custom, but their existing customer base just thinks they act the part very well (assuming the vampire <i>is</i> scrupulous about that stuff, and one would assume they are if they want it as a source of income).<br /> &quot;She's amazing, like the realest experience I've had. I know she creeped you out and all, she always does that - but she always stays in your limits, I've never heard anyone say otherwise. But outside the scene, I wouldn't wanna hang with her - it's like she <i>always</i> in character - brr.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}